<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, we evaluate our method using the array-of-spheres protocol, which renders a grid of diffuse spheres on a ground plane using the predicted environment map.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We use 2,240 perspective crops from 224 Laval Indoor panoramas, provided by DiffusionLight<span id="footnote10" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">10</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/DiffusionLight/image-array_of_spheres" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/DiffusionLight/image-array_of_spheres</a></span></span></span>. All input images are resized to <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512\times 512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>512</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512\times 512</annotation></semantics></math> to match our model input. Quantitative results are shown in Table <a href="#A3.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ C.1 Array-of-Spheres Evaluation ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments ‣ LuxDiT: Lighting Estimation with Video Diffusion Transformer" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and qualitative results in Fig. <a href="#A3.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ C.1 Array-of-Spheres Evaluation ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments ‣ LuxDiT: Lighting Estimation with Video Diffusion Transformer" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">While our method performs slightly below specialized systems like Weber <span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">et al</span>.<span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite> and EMLight <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>]</cite>, it remains competitive—despite not being trained on Laval Indoor. Notably, it outperforms StyleLight <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite> and DiffusionLight <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>, demonstrating strong generalization across lighting domains.</p>
</div>
